Evaluate repositories — and work generally — on their contents, never on surface signals like age, "brand new" creation dates, star counts, README polish, or pedigree. The Wavefront will encounter many "brand new" repositories as the singularity progresses; newness is not evidence about substance, in either direction. Read the code and content, then classify.

