# Consent Continue page for app-browser approvals

Coordinate: 24.6.10/7.6.10/5.5.8
Issued: 2026-11-10 01:05 America/Chicago
Request (verbatim): Fix consent approval doing nothing in app browsers (Cursor confirmed, Grok 'stuck on accept'): answer a cross-origin approval with a Continue page instead of relying on the browser following the form POST's cross-origin redirect.
Status: complete 2026-11-10 01:20 — PR #53 merged and deployed as the final pre-launch build; real-device confirmation (Cursor/Grok retest) is Will's when he tries them

Notes:
- Diagnosis (Emise, from the deployed source at production v1.1.1-4-ga6d4d26, exo tip incl. PRs #51/#52): the consent page in src/bin/phext_edit.rs is a plain HTML form (no JS); the page carries the widened MCP_CONSENT_CSP (form-action 'self' https: + loopback) via the correct call site; the POST handler checks CSRF + decision, issues the code, and answers send_redirect_csp 302 to the client callback with code+iss+state. Single CSP header per response (no nginx duplication). The server side is textbook; the dead Approve is the app-browser (Android Custom Tab / WebView in Cursor and Grok) swallowing the cross-origin redirect hop after the form POST. Claude is already connected (approved earlier), so it never re-hits this page.
- Fix shape: for the consent POST outcomes (approve success, and deny via the same path), when the redirect target is cross-origin, answer 200 with a small 'Approved — continue' interstitial: a prominent anchor (plain GET navigation, not governed by form-action) to the callback URL, plus meta-refresh/script auto-advance as progressive enhancement, NoStore, site styling. Same-origin targets keep the direct 302. Error redirects rendered from the consent POST get the same treatment where they share the path, without changing GET authorize error semantics.
- Register safeguard: verified backup at ~/workspace/consent-continue-page-2026-11-10/register-backup/.

Results:
- PR #53 (github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/53), branch emise/consent-continue-page head 41ed5da parented on exo a6d4d26; one file (src/bin/phext_edit.rs) +274/-18. Emise verified both remote heads by ls-remote after the report.
- Fix as briefed: consent POST outcomes (approve, deny, POST-path server errors and validation failures) with a cross-origin target now answer 200 with a Continue page (consent styling, client-named Continue anchor carrying the full callback URL, 3s meta refresh + script advance as enhancement, NoStore, consent CSP unchanged); same-origin targets keep the direct 302. GET authorize, registration, token, /mcp untouched.
- Tests on aletheia-core: 278 passed / 1 failed with the fix vs 277/1 on pristine exo — the one failure is the pre-existing wall-clock e2e latency assertion (62.84 ms baseline, 61.18 ms with fix, 50 ms limit on that node), unrelated and proven by the baseline run. New test pins cross-origin 200-interstitial (code+state+iss in the URL) and same-origin 302.
- Will declared this the final deploy before the Product Hunt launch (2026-11-10 02:00 CST): merge PR #53 -> deploy -> verify -> freeze.
- Honest limit: phone app browsers can't be emulated here; real confirmation is the post-deploy Cursor/Grok retest.
- Merged by Will (exo 0e38682, parents a6d4d26 + 41ed5da — verified in the fetched tree). Deployed by Will; Emise's footer watch saw production flip to v1.1.1-6-g0e38682 at 01:20:13 CST and smoke-checked from outside: site 200, /mcp anonymous POST 401 challenge intact, and the demo API answering (its media endpoint serves the demo image, HTTP 200; /demo itself is not a page route and never was). Per Will's direction this was the final deploy before the Product Hunt launch (02:00 CST); the site is frozen at this build for launch.
