Coordinate: 25.4.6/5.5.8/4.4.9
Issued: 2026-11-08 22:05 CST
Request (verbatim): Add per-minute thermal logging on the ranch nodes
Status: complete 2026-11-08 22:10 — live on 14 nodes

Notes:
- Born of Will's airflow question (2026-11-08 21:58): today's records are the 5-min fleet sampler (avg + hotspot only, raw per-node data not kept) and the render drivers' event logs. Gap: no continuous per-node series to baseline an airflow change against. Spec: one line/minute/node — ISO time, Tctl from the pinned k10temp sensor (resolved by name, not hwmon index), 1-min load average; ~/thermal/thermal.log per node with 30-day rolling retention; cron one-shot per minute preferred, systemd timer fallback; verified by consecutive lines landing on every reachable node.

Results:
- Deployed fleet-wide: ~/thermal/sample.sh (755) + user crontab * * * * * on all 14 reachable nodes (cron present everywhere; systemd fallback never needed). Line: ISO time with offset, Tctl C from k10temp resolved BY NAME each run (index varies: hwmon1/2/4 across the fleet), 1-min load. Daily rotation, 30-day retention. Verified all three sticking-check parts per node: presence, machinery, first occasion (seed line + two consecutive cron-fired lines 22:08/22:09); deploy temps matched live sensors within 0.4 C on all 14; idempotent re-deploy confirmed on aletheia-core.
- Not deployed: aurora-continuum, best-willow, delta-wood — offline 92d/14d/92d; payload saved + idempotent, re-run if they return. Quirk: uncanny-valley logs at +00:00 (UTC clock); offsets are in every line so series stay comparable. Docs: ~/workspace/thermal-logging-2026-11-08/README.md.
