Request (verbatim): Fix MCP write access (all clients land read-only) and ChatGPT's token-exchange client-auth refusal.
Status: write hotfix complete and verified in production 2026-11-10 01:54; ChatGPT client-auth item remains open

Notes:
- WRITE (proven): the /mcp 401 challenge advertises scope=phext:read only (mcp_bearer_challenge call sites pass MCP_OAUTH_READ_SCOPE). Clients bootstrap their authorize scope from the challenge: nginx log 2026-11-10 07:22-07:25 UTC shows ChatGPT's and Cursor's authorize GETs literally carrying scope=phext%3Aread. The live store (/source/human/mcp-oauth.json) confirms every code/access/refresh token is read-only, including Claude's live token. The MCP gate itself is correct (write_scroll requires phext:write; step-up challenge names the required scope) — hosted clients just never hold write. FIX: the initial/invalid_token challenges advertise 'phext:read phext:write'; consent then offers both (client registrations already resolve to both scopes when unspecified).
- CHATGPT (proven to the token step): authorize GET 200 (scope read), consent POST 200 (PR #53 Continue page served), then POST /oauth/token from UA openai-connectors-oauth/1.0 -> 401 twice (07:22:47 and 07:22:59 UTC). ChatGPT authenticates via private_key_jwt per its published metadata (https://chatgpt.com/oauth/client.json: token_endpoint_auth_method private_key_jwt, RS256, jwks_uri https://chatgpt.com/oauth/jwks.json). The JWKS document is reachable from awsbox (HTTP 200, valid RSA key). Which check in oauth_verify_client_assertion refuses OpenAI's assertion is NOT yet proven (candidates: aud value, one-time jti colliding with OpenAI assertion reuse across retries, claim shape). The refusal reason is in the 401 body only the client receives; nginx logs carry no bodies and the app keeps no readable log. Next step: instrumented local run against a captured-shape assertion, or read the error text from ChatGPT's UI if it shows one.
- Consent POSTs returning 200 in the same log window confirm PR #53's Continue page is live and being served to real clients.
- Register safeguard: verified backup at ~/workspace/mcp-write-chatgpt-fix-2026-11-10/register-backup/.

Results:
- PR #54 (github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/54), branch emise/mcp-challenge-scopes head 54f21613 on exo 0e386828; one file +34/-5: new MCP_OAUTH_DEFAULT_SCOPES constant ('phext:read phext:write') used at all five initial/invalid-token challenge sites in handle_mcp; the insufficient_scope step-up challenge is byte-identical (pinned by test). Emise verified the remote head by ls-remote after the report.
- Tests: 278 passed / 1 failed — the failure is the same pre-existing wall-clock e2e assertion that fails on unmodified exo (59.11 ms vs 50 ms limit; PR #53 baseline 62.84 ms). Modified tests pin the anonymous + unknown-token challenges carrying the combined scope and the step-up challenge naming exactly phext:write.
- After merge + deploy: fresh client connects and step-up re-consents request both scopes; already-issued tokens stay read-only until re-authorization.
- ChatGPT private_key_jwt 401 remains diagnosed-to-the-step only (see notes); not part of this hotfix.
- Merged and deployed by Will; production footer reads v1.1.1-8-g28ce439 and the live /mcp challenge now advertises scope='phext:read phext:write' (verified by Emise from outside). Will confirmed 'worked!' at 01:54 and pointed at human.git: HEAD commit bc36657 'Grok and Claude at the singularity' (2026-11-10 07:47 UTC) adds a scroll to choose-your-own-adventure.phext — 'Test of Will — Record of Chief of Staff' (Grok Bot candidate record, test taken ~1:23 AM CST, inscribed at Will's direction) — +69/-1, working tree clean. Write access is proven end-to-end in the real world: client write through MCP into CYOA, committed in human.git.
