# Organize areas in research.phext — state machines, statements, reference material, the path, researchers; make the Oracle's build structure plain

Coordinate: 30.7.8/9.7.13/7.7.10
Issued: 2026-11-08 13:05 CST
Request (verbatim): Organize areas in research.phext for state machines, statements, reference material, the path we took (the original submission order), and researchers. Ensure that the structure of how the Oracle was built is plain.
Status: complete 2026-11-08

Notes:
- Will-directed restructure (rules 8+14, no pruning): give research.phext five explicit AREAS — (1) State machines: index of every machine extracted under rule 13, stated vs inferred; (2) Statements: the standings area (Ch.1 §4) presented as the statements area with basis legend and transition rules; (3) Reference material: foundations + defined words + standoff companions as the reference area; (4) The path: chronology of intakes in original submission order (papers and studies, dates, NI/OP, passes); (5) Researchers: index of the people behind the ingested works with their chapters and rule-15 standings. Plus a plain-language 'how the Oracle was built' structure scroll. Areas must be generated from the phext's actual contents, carry a maintenance duty (charter rule 16: every ingestion updates the areas), and the pass is logged as Restructure Pass #4.
- DONE — Restructure Pass #4 (logged at 1.1.5). New Ch.1 §5 Areas (1.5.1-1.5.8): 1.5.1 areas map; 1.5.2 State machines (23 entries: 14 extracted under rule 13 — 9 stated, 5 inferred; 9 found-noted from pre-rule-13 chapters, explicitly not upgraded, no gap test; 2 chapters swept with none found); 1.5.3 Statements (door to §4, lists not duplicated); 1.5.4 Reference material (foundations + Defined Words + standoffs); 1.5.5 The path (12 intakes in verified arrival order, NI/axis/OP per paper, passes placed); 1.5.6 Researchers (44 named + Aeneas's 'and others'; only P006/P007/S004 author-checked, the other 41 marked 'not checked — predates rule 15', no verdicts fabricated); 1.5.7-1.5.8 How this Oracle was built (plain structure, honesty boundary stated). Charter rule 16 added (charter scroll + rd-tracker skill): areas carry an upkeep duty — every ingestion/pass updates the areas it touches; a stale area is a defect. Registry 274 = 274 scrolls: True 145 (stipulation 131, verified 14), Unknown 129, False 0, Fiction 0; 8 first standings, zero transitions (path + researchers stand verified on line-by-line checks against the tracker's own records). Lean re-proved over 274 entries (propext only). Final: 274 scrolls, sha256 4f38da62a46e525acf29495a1a4709d26a2c7b6985d6a949f92b3dabac0a7bbc, Singular residual 0. Next restructure due Paper 010 or 100 concepts.
# Thirst for Knowledge quest — daily arXiv math scan, skim-before prediction, skim calibration on the Oracle detection list

