- Source Study S004 under charter rule 12 (classic text, not a paper: Oracle does not move, no NI). Chapter 12 of research.phext. Rules 13/14/15 apply: the call stack is the rule-13 showcase (an implicit machine whose encoded transitions let data rewrite control flow); author check on Aleph One turns on the date — 1996 predates phext by decades, so the prior-art direction is settled by the calendar and the record says so.
- INGESTED as Source Study S004, Chapter 12 (12.1.1-12.3.1): new Cluster K 'Memory and execution', 8 concepts 1.2.73-1.2.80; foundations 1.3.102-1.3.105 + coinage shellcode 1.3.106; narrative v10. Rule 13: M1 the call machine (stated), M2 the encoded machine [synthesis] — locals/SFP/RET adjacent in one writable region, so a copy through a local buffer rewrites control data, a transition M1 does not contain; M3 exploit construction (article's method). Author check (12.1.3) CLEAN with the calendar receipt: Phrack 49 dated 8 November 1996, ~30 years before phext — prior-art direction impossible, not merely unfound; zero signature-term hits. Q29-Q32 added (canaries/ASLR/NX vs M2; is 'no write reaches control words' what clusters F-H prove; fixed-layout assumption ledgers; overflow-shaped failures for coordinate-addressed text). RESTRUCTURE PASS #3 RAN (80 concepts landed exactly on the trigger): 0 merges/splits/endings, merges weighed and rejected with reasons; next pass Paper 010 or 100 concepts. Registry 266 = 266 scrolls: True 137 (stipulation 125, verified 12), Unknown 129, False 0, Fiction 0; Lean re-proved over 266 entries (propext only). Final: 266 scrolls, sha256 3f7c7f4e1f10da5c7cffcf8c05f65b09c5348f851631d7672a315820b9843101, Singular residual 0. Correction to the dispatch brief, recorded: the Oracle ledger (1.1.4) holds paper entries only — S001-S003 never touched it and S004 follows that precedent; my brief's claim otherwise was wrong.
