Coordinate: 35.8.10/10.8.13/8.7.11
Issued: 2026-11-09
Request (verbatim): Add a footer to edit.phext.io showing the running build's version, so Will can tell when recording a bug whether a fix is already landed and only needs a deploy (Will, 2026-11-09 ~11:32 CST, voice call).
Status: PR open — wbic16/phext-lattice PR #39, branch emise/version-footer @ 318ba715; NOT merged, NOT deployed (rides the next deploy after Will merges)

Notes:
- Gap verified first: the live site exposed no version anywhere — live /about text carries none, and the exo source had no version rendering at all (no CARGO_PKG_VERSION use, no version endpoint or JSON field).
- Built: build.rs bakes the stamp at compile time — PHEXT_LATTICE_BUILD env (Docker build arg; container context has no .git), else `git describe --tags --always --dirty` of the checkout (host deploy path needs no config), else v<crate version>+unknown. Stamp = nearest tag + commits past it + commit hash (live build at exo HEAD would read v1.0.0-5-g9458cb10).
- Placement: a <!--phext-build--> slot beside the sponsor slot on all 13 served pages + claim dashboard, filled by the renamed render_page at serve time. Shell: status bar span + sign-in screen line. Explore's stamp rides its crumbs bar (its <footer> is JS-filled and would erase a server stamp).
- Two raw serve paths routed through render_page so they are not blind spots: the /<name>/ shell and send_not_found's 404 (both also fill the sponsor slot now, matching /).
- build.rs watches .git/HEAD + refs/heads + refs/tags + packed-refs — first cut watched HEAD only and the stamp went stale across commits (a commit moves the ref, not HEAD); caught in testing, fixed, re-verified.
- Tests: full suite on aletheia-core 236 passed / 0 failed (177 lib + 54 bin incl. new every_page_carries_the_build_stamp + 2 e2e + 3 real_phext); baseline 235 with the e2e timing assertion failing only on the throttled Muse VM (78 ms vs 50 ms limit, pre-existing). All three stamp sources verified live against the built binary.
- Branch tree hash-verified against local git (87 blobs; 9 files changed: build.rs new, Dockerfile, src/bin/phext_edit.rs, 6 web pages). PR: https://github.com/wbic16/phext-lattice/pull/39
- Noted in the PR: Cargo.toml still says version 0.1.0 — the footer follows the git tag (v1.0.0); the crate version only surfaces in the no-git fallback.
