Coordinate: 38.6.9/7.5.9/5.5.10
Issued: 2026-11-09 11:26 CST
Request (verbatim): Will's ruling on the 2026-11-09 voice call: run the fix pass and get wbic16/neovim PR #1 green; sync the fork with upstream; fork CI is nice-to-have, not a must-have — disable a check rather than fight it if it cannot reasonably be fixed. Merge stays Will's.
Status: blocked on GitHub Actions account state — tree verified green locally and on prior head (38/39, sole failure a no-failing-test windows flake); fresh CI cannot execute until Actions runs jobs again on wbic16's account

Notes:
- Triage vs upstream baseline: all 13 red checks on the original head cf7eeb60 were PR-caused except wasm (pre-existing upstream: the wasm build fails identically on upstream master dca26833 and on the pre-patch base c868e1ab — zig fetch of lua.org times out; it also passed on the rebased head without any action).
- Root cause of 11 red checks (functionaltest x7 flavours, windows functional, zig linux+macos): one functional test — test/functional/plugin/phext_spec.lua 'deletes an emptied scroll...' — used ... inside a nested IIFE where varargs are out of scope. Fixed by binding the path first. Verified locally: spec 11/11 PASSED before and after the rebase.
- lint fixed in the plugin's own files: emmylua --warnings-as-errors went 51 warnings -> 0 (nil-guards/asserts on index lookups, new PhextEffIndex class for the effective index, non-deprecated window sizing via nvim_win_set_config, ftplugin option set via :append, annotations). StyLua: CI installs StyLua latest (2.6.0); the phext spec was reformatted with 2.6.0 — upstream files that 'fail' under StyLua 2.3.x pass under 2.6.0 untouched.
- docs fixed in runtime/doc/phext.txt (invalid tag links |mP|/|phext-next|/|phext-step| re-pointed to real anchors, Neovim->Nvim spelling per lintdoc spell_dict, proper h1 title) — make doc + make lintdoc + linterrcodes all rc=0 locally, docs check green in CI.
- news check fixed: FEATURES entry for phext added to runtime/doc/news.txt EDITOR section (the PR's only hunk in an upstream file; recorded in PATCHES.md).
- lintcommit caught a real defect in the fix pass itself: commit type 'style' is not in upstream's allowed list — reworded to 'fix' before final push (local lintcommit run clean).
- Fork sync: fork master fast-forwarded c868e1ab -> dca26833 (17 upstream commits); PR branch rebased onto dca26833, old tip preserved on backup/emise-phext-support-20261109-pre-rebase, force-with-lease per Will's rebase rule. PATCHES.md base record updated.
- Commits on the branch: fa4d0895d feat (original, rebased), f8d5d4c68 fix (CI green pass), 191952530 fix (stylua 2.6), de2c34eee docs (PATCHES.md). Head at record time: 7b5147e2e (de2c34eee plus the PATCHES fresh-eyes note commit, a docs-only roll to re-run the flaked windows job).
- Nothing was disabled: no workflow or check was turned off — every red check was either fixed or proven pre-existing/transient (wasm). PR #1 NOT merged (Will's act).
- Windows functional flake (2026-11-09): the de2c34eee run failed with NO failing test — all 18 groups passed; its terminal parallel group exited 1 while reporting 490 passed / 51 skipped / 0 failed (harness-level exit; the group carries many recorded Windows flake skips; the same tree passed the same job on head f8d5d4c68; phext spec ran 11/11 OK inside the failing job). Not PR-caused and not a code defect.
- BLOCKER — GitHub Actions stopped executing on the fork (2026-11-09 ~12:27 CST): to re-run the flaked job, the head was rolled with docs-only commit 7b5147e2e (PATCHES.md fresh-eyes note; spec 11/11 + stylua 2.6 + lintcommit target all re-verified locally first; old tips preserved on backup/emise-phext-support-20261109-pre-roll and backup/emise-phext-support-20261109-pre-reword-69632fa8). Every workflow on the new head then 'failed' in ~52s with ZERO jobs created (11 runs, 0 jobs total; only the VM-based FreeBSD check ran). This jobless instant-failure pattern is the signature of Actions being unable to start jobs on the account — most consistent with exhausted monthly Actions minutes/billing on wbic16's account (the fix pass alone burned ~241 wall-clock minutes of runs on 2026-11-09, large Windows/macOS jobs at premium multipliers; the billing endpoint is not readable with the fork token, so the account-side cause is Will's to confirm in GitHub Settings > Billing). Nothing in the pushed tree can cause zero-job failures across unrelated workflows including codeql/label-pr/build_dummy. ACTIONS FOR WILL: (1) check/fix Actions billing or wait for the quota reset; (2) then re-run the failed workflows on PR #1 (or push any commit) — the tree is verified and expected to go green; windows functional may still flake occasionally (upstream-known).

